{title: 329 - Take the World, but Give Me Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #329 • TAKE THE WORLD BUT GIVE  • 15.15.15.15}
{lyricist: Fanny J. Crosby}
{composer: John R. Sweney}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 329}
{meta: tune TAKE THE WORLD BUT GIVE }
{meta: meter 15.15.15.15}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Take the world, [F/C]but give me [C]Jesus, All its [C7]joys are but a name;
[C7]But His love abideth [Dm/A]ever, Through [F/C]eternal [C]years the same.
[C]Oh, the [C7]height and depth of mercy! Oh, the length and breadth of [Dm/A]love!
[Am]Oh, the fullness [Bb]of redemption, Pledge [Am]of endless life above!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]Oh, the [Dm]height and depth of [C]mercy!
[Dm/A]Oh, the length [F/C]and breadth [C]of love!
[C]Oh, the [C7]fullness of redemption,
[C7]Pledge of endless life above.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Take the [F/C]world, [C]but give me [C7]Jesus,
[C7]Sweetest comfort [Dm/A]of [F/C]my [C]soul;
[C]With [C7]my Savior watching o'er me,
[Am]I can [Bb]sing, though [Am]billows roll.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Take the [F/C]world, [C]but give me [C7]Jesus;
[C7]Let me view [Dm/A]his constant [F/C]smile;
[C]Then [C7]throughout my pilgrim journey
[Am]Light will [Bb]cheer me all [Am]the while.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]Take the [F/C]world, [C]but give me [C7]Jesus;
[C7]In His cross [Dm/A]my trust [F/C]shall [C]be,
[C]Till, [C7]with clearer, brighter vision
[Am]Face to [Bb]face my [Am]Lord I see.
{end_of_verse}
